/* Roupagens: the stories of the map generator. The mechanics of a generated map are fixed (pieces that unlock a door,
   something that calls waves, a guide to escort, captives to free, a clock); a skin is the story dressing of one of them,
   drawn BEFORE the map is built, with its own placement rules:
   - tags of every skin: f (factions), t (themes), a (acts: [2] needs the second box), p (premises); [] = any;
   - portadores: the kinds of object that may carry it, in order (a key in a chest, a lever only on a token, a captive under
     the wagon); reaproveita: may it be found in an object already in the room; veste: the thing IS the object (its look
     replaces the object's look) or lies inside/under it.
   A skin is not repeated within a campaign while others fit. The whole file is data: exportable and importable (Map
   generator > Stories), and made by tools/montar_historias.py from editor/historias/bigorna-historias.json. Since v5 each
   element carries "narrativa" (its narrative role: function, what it causes, its consequences, its links to elements of
   other families with a strength) and HISTORIAS.narrativa holds the grammar (arcs, events, transitions, pacing rules).
   Placeholders: {vilao} {lugar} {alvo} {n} {w} {vN} {oque} {Oque} {X} {limite} {desde} {preco} {hero1}; [n] and [total] in
   counter lines. Portuguese: "de {vilao}" becomes "do …" by itself (contrair). */
